-   entry .Frame   an HTTP/2 frame: a nine-byte header and a type-specific payload, decoded from and serialised to bytes
+   entry .Frame   una trama HTTP/2: una cabecera de nueve bytes y una carga útil específica del tipo, decodificada desde bytes y serializada a bytes

=   entry .Frame   an HTTP/2 frame: a nine-byte header and a type-specific payload, decoded from and serialised to bytes
-     detail
+     detail

-         The wire unit of HTTP/2 (RFC 7540 §4): a 24-bit length, an 8-bit type, 8 flag bits, a
-         31-bit stream id, and a payload whose shape the type decides. `Frame` is an enum of the
-         types the engine models, each case holding its decoded fields rather than raw flags:
+         La unidad de transmisión de HTTP/2 (RFC 7540 §4): una longitud de 24 bits, un tipo de 8
+         bits, 8 bits de indicadores, un identificador de flujo de 31 bits y una carga útil cuya
+         forma decide el tipo. `Frame` es una enumeración de los tipos que modela el motor, en la
+         que cada caso contiene sus campos decodificados en lugar de indicadores en bruto:

-         ```tabular
+         ```tabular

-         column  Case
-         column  Frame
-         row  `Headers(streamId, headerBlock, endStream, endHeaders)`  an HPACK block, with padding and any `PRIORITY` prefix already stripped
-         row  `Continuation(streamId, headerBlock, endHeaders)`  the rest of a block too large for one `HEADERS` frame
-         row  `Data(streamId, payload, endStream)`  body bytes, padding stripped
-         row  `RstStream(streamId, errorCode)`  the peer abandoning a stream
-         row  `Settings(settings, ack)`  a list of `Setting`s, or an empty acknowledgement
-         row  `Ping(opaque, ack)`  eight opaque bytes, echoed back with `ack`
-         row  `GoAway(lastStreamId, errorCode, debug)`  the peer closing the connection
-         row  `WindowUpdate(streamId, increment)`  flow-control credit, for the connection on stream `0`
-         row  `Ignored(typeId, streamId)`  an inbound frame of a type the engine does not model (`PRIORITY`, `PUSH_PROMISE`, an extension), decoded only to be discarded, as the protocol requires; it can never be serialised
+         column  Caso
+         column  Trama
+         row  `Headers(streamId, headerBlock, endStream, endHeaders)`  un bloque HPACK, con el relleno y cualquier prefijo `PRIORITY` ya eliminados
+         row  `Continuation(streamId, headerBlock, endHeaders)`  el resto de un bloque demasiado grande para una sola trama `HEADERS`
+         row  `Data(streamId, payload, endStream)`  bytes del cuerpo, sin el relleno
+         row  `RstStream(streamId, errorCode)`  el interlocutor abandona un flujo
+         row  `Settings(settings, ack)`  una lista de `Setting`s, o un acuse de recibo vacío
+         row  `Ping(opaque, ack)`  ocho bytes opacos, que se devuelven con `ack`
+         row  `GoAway(lastStreamId, errorCode, debug)`  el interlocutor cierra la conexión
+         row  `WindowUpdate(streamId, increment)`  crédito de control de flujo, para la conexión en el flujo `0`
+         row  `Ignored(typeId, streamId)`  una trama entrante de un tipo que el motor no modela (`PRIORITY`, `PUSH_PROMISE`, una extensión), decodificada solo para descartarla, como exige el protocolo; nunca puede serializarse

=         row  `Ignored(typeId, streamId)`  an inbound frame of a type the engine does not model (`PRIORITY`, `PUSH_PROMISE`, an extension), decoded only to be discarded, as the protocol requires; it can never be serialised
-         ```
+         ```

